<section class="notebook"><article class="research-note" id="llm-wiki"><div><span class="maturity">Private research workflow</span><h2>LLM Wiki</h2></div><div><p>A source-backed knowledge workflow inspired by Andrej Karpathy’s LLM Wiki pattern: keep original sources, connect working notes, and carry citations into the synthesis.</p><p>No public release. The working collection is private; its notes, operational records, and source files are not published here.</p><a class="text-link" href="/methodology">The evidence principle ↗</a></div></article><article class="research-note"><div><p class="eyebrow">Reading the labels</p><h2>Source ≠ finished.</h2></div><div><p><strong>Public source</strong> means there is a repository to inspect, not a supported hosted service. <strong>Early alpha</strong> means a narrow foundation exists and significant capabilities are still missing. <strong>Local prototype</strong> means local implementation, without a public release.</p><p>Descriptions are based on inspected project documentation. This site does not independently certify every capability or publish benchmark claims.</p><a class="text-link" href="/labs">Historical notes & corrections ↗</a></div></article></section></main><Footer/></Layout>
